{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UDsGxnFyXnFX1xA68nRLG4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific detailed reviewer guidelines and review forms for 2026 were not directly available in the results. However, I can provide you with what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Information\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US, and it is an annual international conference bringing together the robotics and machine learning research communities, focusing on the increasingly important role of learning in robotics with the aim to publish significant original research at the intersection of robotics and machine learning.\n\n## Reviewer-Related Requirements\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nFor specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and the detailed review form, you would need to check:\n- The official CoRL 2026 website (corl.org)\n- The OpenReview platform at: https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\n\nThe search results included historical reviewer guidelines from CoRL 2023 and 2024, but the 2026-specific review form and guidelines may not yet be publicly available or may be provided directly to assigned reviewers through OpenReview.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1daec3f0-5eda-4fd1-9945-e0c719d586e4","uuid":"2df6a50a-7455-45c0-8412-117e528b14be","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:16:15.606Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01GxBJQTfre1r59ygFKHniSN","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific detailed reviewer guidelines and review forms for 2026 were not directly available in the results. However, I can provide you with what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Information\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US, and it is an annual international conference bringing together the robotics and machine learning research communities, focusing on the increasingly important role of learning in robotics with the aim to publish significant original research at the intersection of robotics and machine learning.\n\n## Reviewer-Related Requirements\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nFor specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and the detailed review form, you would need to check:\n- The official CoRL 2026 website (corl.org)\n- The OpenReview platform at: https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\n\nThe search results included historical reviewer guidelines from CoRL 2023 and 2024, but the 2026-specific review form and guidelines may not yet be publicly available or may be provided directly to assigned reviewers through OpenReview."],"durationSeconds":7.36376195}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NZGMPthBbu259GeP6Q5BzN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review criteria scoring rubric\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11000557/\"},{\"title\":\"Evaluating Applications Under NIH's Simplified Review ...\",\"url\":\"https://edgeforscholars.vumc.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Simplified-Review-Reviewer-Guide-to-Evaluating-Applications.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Beyond Paper-to-Paper: Structured Profiling and Rubric Scoring for Paper-Reviewer Matching\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.05866\"}]\n\nThe search results include information about NeurIPS 2025 and CoRL 2024 reviewer guidelines, but not specifically CoRL 2025 guidelines. Let me search more specifically for CoRL 2025 information.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"RemembeRL - Workshop @ CoRL 2025\",\"url\":\"https://rememberl-corl25.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 - Instruction for Presentations\",\"url\":\"https://2025.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-presentations\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"}]\n\nLet me search specifically for CoRL 2025 instruction for reviews:\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Workshop Open Hardware | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FWorkshop%2FOpen_Hardware\"},{\"title\":\"LEAP: Learning Effective Abstractions for Planning | CoRL 2025\",\"url\":\"https://leap-workshop.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 - Instruction for Presentations\",\"url\":\"https://2025.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-presentations\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - smallfryy/corl-2025-papers: ✨ 200+ robotics papers from CoRL 2025, with TLDRs, project pages, code, and more\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/smallfryy/corl-2025-papers\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos\"},{\"title\":\"Can LLM feedback enhance review quality? A randomized study of 20K   reviews at ICLR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.09737\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056528/\"}]\n\nLet me try searching for the CoRL 2025 website directly with reviewer instructions:\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://2025.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 - Instruction for Presentations\",\"url\":\"https://2025.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-presentations\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 - Workshops\",\"url\":\"https://2025.corl.org/program/workshops\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 - Awards\",\"url\":\"https://2025.corl.org/program/awards\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 - Special Panel\",\"url\":\"https://2025.corl.org/program/special-panel\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I was unable to find a publicly available document specifically for \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review criteria scoring rubric.\" \n\nThe search results show that CoRL 2025 has already concluded (the conference took place recently), and while I found the CoRL 2024 reviewer guidelines that cover review criteria, I could not locate a specific CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines document.\n\nFrom the CoRL 2024 guidance that was available, submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical, and results are judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\nIf you need the specific CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines, I recommend:\n1. Checking the CoRL 2025 website directly at 2025.corl.org for any downloadable reviewer documents\n2. Contacting the CoRL 2025 Program Committee or organizers directly\n3. Checking OpenReview (openreview.net) where CoRL submissions are managed, as guidelines may be posted there\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1daec3f0-5eda-4fd1-9945-e0c719d586e4","uuid":"554b0f81-ef6b-4289-bb6b-b4667a4a3935","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:16:20.460Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review criteria scoring rubric","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KL69ac9JzWEyQXGHvPUVXz","content":[{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instr