{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XJVvASa4iY61VfANE6FxD2","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:2024.corl.org instruction for reviews\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Call for Workshops\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/call-for-workshops\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Papers XX\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/papers-xx\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instructions for Presentations\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instructions-for-presentations\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Speakers\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/speakers\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Demos\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/demos\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Workshops\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/workshops\"}]\n\nI found the \"Instructions for Reviews\" page on the CoRL 2024 website. Here's a summary of the key information:\n\n## Evaluation Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical, and will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\n## Review Process\n\nAuthors of regular paper submissions will have an opportunity to submit a response to reviewers and update the papers during the rebuttal period. Reviews and rebuttals of accepted papers will be made publicly available.\n\nACs will identify the desk rejection candidates, using one of the criteria below as a justification, and the PC will examine the candidates and make the final decision.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nReviewers need to have expertise in robotics, robot learning, machine learning and complementary fields, as demonstrated by a record of previous publications in the area. Reviewers ideally have a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences and journals (e.g. CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, IJRR, TRO, RAL) and core machine learning venues (e.g. NeurIPS, ICML, AIStats, JMLR, PAMI).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1daec3f0-5eda-4fd1-9945-e0c719d586e4","uuid":"718d6742-6c0d-4f0d-a340-867787984de4","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:16:30.599Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:2024.corl.org instruction for reviews","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01AQrLNymgwpsZYrTaH1czdR","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Call for Workshops","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/call-for-workshops"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Call for Papers","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Papers XX","url":"https://2024.corl.org/program/papers-xx"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instructions for Presentations","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instructions-for-presentations"},{"title":"CoRL 2024","url":"https://2024.corl.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Speakers","url":"https://2024.corl.org/program/speakers"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Demos","url":"https://2024.corl.org/program/demos"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Workshops","url":"https://2024.corl.org/program/workshops"}]},"I found the \"Instructions for Reviews\" page on the CoRL 2024 website. Here's a summary of the key information:\n\n## Evaluation Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical, and will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\n## Review Process\n\nAuthors of regular paper submissions will have an opportunity to submit a response to reviewers and update the papers during the rebuttal period. Reviews and rebuttals of accepted papers will be made publicly available.\n\nACs will identify the desk rejection candidates, using one of the criteria below as a justification, and the PC will examine the candidates and make the final decision.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nReviewers need to have expertise in robotics, robot learning, machine learning and complementary fields, as demonstrated by a record of previous publications in the area. Reviewers ideally have a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences and journals (e.g. CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, IJRR, TRO, RAL) and core machine learning venues (e.g. NeurIPS, ICML, AIStats, JMLR, PAMI)."],"durationSeconds":6.490451370000002}}
