{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LpxTXrXUqhPyKiVgCb84Bo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL openreview \"overall score\" \"strong accept\" \"accept\" \"reject\" review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Default Review Form | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"An Open Review of OpenReview: A Critical Analysis of the Machine   Learning Conference Review Process\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.05137\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2017 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2017/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about review forms and scoring systems for CoRL. Here are the key findings:\n\n## OpenReview Default Review Form\n\nThe default OpenReview review form uses a rating scale with integer values from 1-10, where 9 is described as \"Top 15% of accepted papers, strong accept,\" 8 is \"Top 50% of accepted papers, clear accept,\" and 7 is \"Good paper, accept.\"\n\n## CoRL Specific Guidance\n\nCoRL papers that do not receive at least one score of weak accept or above from either a reviewer or the Area Chair will be candidates for first-round rejection without rebuttal. This indicates that CoRL uses acceptance categories including \"weak accept\" and likely other acceptance tiers in their review process.\n\nThe search results show that OpenReview provides a detailed numerical scoring system for reviews, and CoRL uses this platform with specific decision criteria for papers based on review scores.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1daec3f0-5eda-4fd1-9945-e0c719d586e4","uuid":"8890bc0a-065f-4349-82d1-4a19f1e88563","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:17:06.625Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL openreview \"overall score\" \"strong accept\" \"accept\" \"reject\" review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01FFr1ThKQrMXjx9er7Tv5uA","content":[{"title":"Default Review Form | OpenReview","url":"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/"},{"title":"An Open Review of OpenReview: A Critical Analysis of the Machine   Learning Conference Review Process","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.05137"},{"title":"ICML 2017 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2017/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/"}]},"I found relevant information about review forms and scoring systems for CoRL. Here are the key findings:\n\n## OpenReview Default Review Form\n\nThe default OpenReview review form uses a rating scale with integer values from 1-10, where 9 is described as \"Top 15% of accepted papers, strong accept,\" 8 is \"Top 50% of accepted papers, clear accept,\" and 7 is \"Good paper, accept.\"\n\n## CoRL Specific Guidance\n\nCoRL papers that do not receive at least one score of weak accept or above from either a reviewer or the Area Chair will be candidates for first-round rejection without rebuttal. This indicates that CoRL uses acceptance categories including \"weak accept\" and likely other acceptance tiers in their review process.\n\nThe search results show that OpenReview provides a detailed numerical scoring system for reviews, and CoRL uses this platform with specific decision criteria for papers based on review scores."],"durationSeconds":8.464379826000004}}
