{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cu9dutShfXCtiaf8kavghg","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/paper/appendix.tex:1096:The $2 {\\times} 2$ trained-vs-reference comparison reveals a consistent reorganization pattern: reference OpenVLA collapses from L0 ($R^2 = 0.629$) to near-zero at mid-layers (L20: $0.086$, std $= 0.277$), while reference Phi-3-V peaks at L6 ($0.578$) with gradual decline (std $= 0.068$)---qualitatively opposite reference landscapes.\ndocs/paper/appendix.tex:1106:\\paragraph{Observational three-tier gradient.}\ndocs/paper/appendix.tex:1107:The cross-architecture matrix suggests a three-tier gradient of representational adaptation.\ndocs/paper/appendix.tex:1112:Testing additional general-purpose VLAs (e.g., Octo~\\cite{ghosh2024_octo}, $\\pi_0$~\\cite{black2024_pi0}) at Tier~2 is necessary before the three-tier structure can be treated as a robust empirical pattern.\ndocs/paper/appendix.tex:1141:The three-tier gradient has $n = 1$ at Tier~2, limiting its inferential power; populating this tier with additional general-purpose VLAs is a priority for future work.\ndocs/paper/appendix.tex:1275:Table~\\ref{tab:convergent_evidence} summarizes what each method measures, its key finding, evidence type, and acknowledged limitation.\ndocs/paper/appendix.tex:1280:\\label{tab:convergent_evidence}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01TM3u5QfQkhWB8okD6Pp3QB","session_id":"1daec3f0-5eda-4fd1-9945-e0c719d586e4","uuid":"b2c17472-9db1-4103-9f21-72a293404229","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:19:43.196Z"}
